		description: "Atomically changes the slug, creates a 301 redirect, and retargets inbound chains to the final public URL. Returns 409 when another record currently owns the new slug (slug-held-by-record) or a redirect row already claims its public path (slug-held-by-redirect). Company-class entity slugs keep the HQ location suffix; Product and Service slugs stay scoped to their provider pair: a rename may reuse a slug held by another provider's offering and returns 409 only for a same-provider sibling, a non-product holder, or a redirect owning the provider-scoped path.",
